{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right square pyramid has a total surface area of <math alttext=\"70,560\"><mn>70,560</mn>\n</math> square inches, and the combined surface area of the four lateral faces of this pyramid is <math alttext=\"38,160\"><mn>38,160</mn>\n</math> square inches. What is the height, in inches, of this pyramid?</p>", "keys": ["5f58c671-a8d8-4cc6-a3ff-c1d23097752b"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "5f58c671-a8d8-4cc6-a3ff-c1d23097752b", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "8006fa49-1722-4f5a-81cf-6844eab366b6", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "6fe9016e-d61e-436a-8556-6d779b9f76a0", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"106\"><mn>106</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "3ac1d953-2d8a-40ca-a156-5d02ed375b7f", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The total surface area of a right square pyramid is the sum of the combined surface area of its four lateral faces and the area of its square base. It&rsquo;s given that the right square pyramid has a total surface area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70,560\"><mn>70,560</mn></math> square inches, and the combined surface area of the four lateral faces of this pyramid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"38,160\"><mn>38,160</mn></math> square inches. It follows that the area of the square base is the difference between the total surface area and the combined surface area of the four lateral faces, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 70,560 minus 38,160 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>70,560</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>38,160</mn><mo>)</mo></math> square inches, which is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"32,400\"><mn>32,400</mn></math> square inches. The area,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi></math>, of the base of a square pyramid is given by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B equals s squared\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is the side length of the base. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"32,400\"><mn>32,400</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"32,400 equals s squared\"><mn>32,400</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the positive square root of both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180 equals s\"><mn>180</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></math>. The four lateral faces of a square pyramid are congruent triangles. It follows that the area of each lateral face is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 38,160 Over 4 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>38,160</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> , or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9,540\"><mn>9,540</mn></math>, square inches. The area,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>,&nbsp;of each lateral face of a square pyramid is given by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half s script l\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is the side length of the pyramid&rsquo;s base and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> is the pyramid&rsquo;s slant height. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9,540\"><mn>9,540</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9,540 equals one half left parenthesis 180 right parenthesis script l\"><mn>9,540</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9,540 equals 90 script l\"><mn>9,540</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"106 equals script l\"><mn>106</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>. In the right square pyramid, a right triangle can be drawn, where the lengths of the legs correspond to the pyramid's height, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, and half the side length of its base, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half s\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>s</mi></math>, and the length of the hypotenuse corresponds to the pyramid's slant height, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>. It follows that the relationship between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h squared plus left parenthesis one half s right parenthesis squared equals script l squared\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"106\"><mn>106</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h squared plus left parenthesis left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 180 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared equals left parenthesis 106 right parenthesis squared\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>106</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h squared plus 8,100 equals 11,236\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8,100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11,236</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8,100\"><mn>8,100</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h squared equals 3,136\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3,136</mn></math>. Taking the positive square root of both sides of the equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals 56\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn></math>. Therefore, the height, in inches, of this pyramid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the pyramid's slant height, not its height, in inches.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the side length of the pyramid's base, not its height, in inches.</p>", "externalid": "d6c651bd-349f-4a16-89ba-e8bb62e72076", "correct_answer": ["A"]}